# Turbo Pascal 6.0 archive - .gitignore
#
# Source (.PAS, .INC), own data formats (.MEN, .CMP, .SND, .PRW, .TPP,
# .NOT, .VOC, .SPT, .DAT, .PCX) and the README.TXT files are tracked.
# Note: .TPP here is the archive's own raw picture format written by
# PCXTOOLS\PCX_PAS.PAS, not a Turbo Pascal protected-mode unit.

# --- Compiler output -------------------------------------------------
*.EXE
*.COM
*.TPU
*.OBJ
*.OVR
*.OVL
*.MAP

# --- Turbo Pascal IDE: editor backups, temp files, desktop/config -----
*.BAK
*.$$$
*.DSK
*.TP
*.PSM

# --- Borland proprietary files shipped with Turbo Pascal --------------
# The BGI\ folder and the copies of its drivers and fonts next to the
# graphics programs. The root README.TXT lists what was there.
/BGI/
*.BGI
*.CHR
# Run-time library, help file, online help index
*.TPL
*.TPH
TURBO.*

# --- Third-party software found among the sources ---------------------
# MS-DOS system file and mouse driver
/SONSTIGE/IO.SYS
/SONSTIGE/MOUSE.SYS
# Tools unrelated to the sports day program (HPTRANS.EXE, F2400.EXE
# and NE.COM are already covered above)
/SPORTTAG/HPTRANS.CFG
# Microsoft Anti-Virus checksum file
CHKLIST.MS

# --- Operating system clutter -----------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Executables without surviving source -----------------------------
# These binaries are the only remaining form of their programs and are
# deliberately not tracked; reconstructing their source is a task for
# later. Uncomment a line to keep that binary despite the *.EXE rule.
#!/MASTER/MMIND.EXE
#!/MASTER/MASTER.EXE
#!/ASTRO/ASTRO.EXE
#!/OBERFL/WIN.EXE
#!/SNDBLS/HOOK.EXE
#!/COMPOSER/COMPTEST.EXE
